<task id="204d" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Class-B B11 staging-slot shadow-worker defect — verify `.Api` split status + complete `.Core/.Api/.Worker` split OR slot-sticky Enabled flags (DS-3 §5)</title>
    <phase>Pre-Live-Fire — Class-B architectural refactor (post-186 safe)</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Structural refactor of L2 control-plane topology — high blast radius (touches project structure, deploy topology, Bicep slot config). Per root CLAUDE.md §8: `l2-controlplane` + `deploy` + architectural-refactor = FULL rigor. Publish-slot semantic changes are irreversible-adjacent (wrong split can silently double-process on production traffic).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Per root CLAUDE.md §8.5: structural refactor + high-blast-radius = Opus/Fable. The choice between "complete `.Core/.Api/.Worker` split" vs "add slot-sticky Enabled flags per DS-3 §5" is architectural — depends on judgment about deploy-topology invariants + operational-simplicity trade-offs. Sonnet insufficient for this architectural judgment call.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches project-file boundaries (`.csproj`, `Program.cs`, Bicep slot config). Concurrent 204a/b/c edits to Worker + Core would race with any reorganization.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>202</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, architectural-refactor, deploy, class-b-verified-open, staging-slot-topology</tags>
    <estimated-effort>16 hours (per punch list B11 estimate — may split into verify-then-refactor if `.Api` already split)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Resolve the B11 staging-slot shadow-worker defect surfaced in DS-3: one-process L2 topology has structural defect where reconciler + crash-recovery + dispatcher run against PRODUCTION Cosmos+SB while a pre-production build is deployed to the staging slot (both slots share config). FIRST STEP: verify `.Api` project split status (Task 202 verification matrix says `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core` + `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker` are separate; `.Api` split status unverified). Two paths:
- **Path SPLIT** (preferred if not done): Complete `.Core+.Api+.Worker` split per DS-3 pattern — `.Api` hosts REST endpoints only (public-facing, ok on both slots), `.Worker` hosts dispatcher+reconciler+crash-recovery (deployed to production slot only, staging slot has no Worker).
- **Path FLAGS**: If split proves impractical, add three permanent slot-sticky `Enabled` config flags (per DS-3 §5 alternative) to Worker: `Dispatcher:Enabled` / `Reconciler:Enabled` / `CrashRecovery:Enabled` — set true on production slot, false on staging slot; startup gate checks flags before instantiating background services.

Choose Path SPLIT if `.Api` is close to done; Path FLAGS if split is heavier than punch list's 16h estimate.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Expert in: DS-3 staging-slot topology analysis + §5 alternatives; ASP.NET Core BackgroundService lifecycle + IHostedService startup gates; App Service slot configuration (`slotSetting: true` semantics); Bicep slot configuration; L2 control-plane project structure (`Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core` + `.Worker` + potentially `.Api`); dispatcher + reconciler + crash-recovery service registrations (`Worker/Program.cs` + `DispatchModule` + `StateReconcilerService`).</role>

  <goal>Either:
- Path SPLIT: `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Api` project exists, hosts REST endpoints only; `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker` hosts dispatcher + reconciler + crash-recovery only; Bicep deploys `.Api` to both slots + `.Worker` to production slot only (or `.Api` includes `.Worker` as optional dep with slot-sticky flag); staging slot startup does NOT instantiate Worker background services; existing tests pass; deploy topology documented in `design.md` §Deploy Topology.
- Path FLAGS: three slot-sticky `Enabled` flags added to Worker configuration; `Program.cs` startup gate checks flags before `.AddHostedService()`; Bicep `slotSetting: true` markers on all three flags with production=true / staging=false; existing tests pass; startup gate has unit tests covering "flag=false skips service" behavior; deploy topology documented.

Either path: staging slot deployment does NOT process production SB messages or Cosmos writes; punch list B11 annotated `applied — Path SPLIT|FLAGS — <evidence>`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-3 (design-study-3, staging-slot topology) surfaced this defect: L2's one-process topology has reconciler polling Cosmos on a timer + crash-recovery scanning SB dead-letters on startup + dispatcher consuming SB session messages. When staging slot is deployed for a pre-production build test, its process ALSO connects to production Cosmos + SB (both slots share `sprk-provisioning-jobs` queue + `sprk-provisioning-state` Cosmos), producing:
- Reconciler double-writes (staging + production both apply the same Cosmos updates on the same timer)
- Crash-recovery false triggers (staging startup thinks production runs crashed)
- Dispatcher double-consume (staging + production both compete for SB session locks — one wins, other silently fails)

**Why post-186 safe (per punch list)**: task 186 first-real-run uses production slot only — no staging slot deployment planned during acceptance. Defect is ACCEPTED for first run + MUST-FIX before ongoing production traffic (staging deploys will start racing production data).

**Path SPLIT is architecturally cleaner** — `.Worker` only in one slot means no runtime flag gymnastics.

**Path FLAGS is operationally simpler** — no project restructure, one process everywhere, config-driven.

**Owner choice may apply**: this is judgment. Task 202 amendment defers to executor's grep-verify: if `.Api` split is close to done (Worker already split), finish it (Path SPLIT); if starting from scratch, Path FLAGS may be pragmatic.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="input">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-202-punch-list.md B11 row + verification matrix</file>
