      <file role="verify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Api/*.csproj (confirm `.Api` split status — MAY NOT EXIST YET)</file>
      <file role="modify-path-SPLIT">src/server/services/ (project restructure: create .Api if missing; move REST endpoints from Worker/Core to .Api)</file>
      <file role="modify-path-FLAGS">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Program.cs (add startup-gate flag reads before AddHostedService)</file>
      <file role="modify-path-FLAGS">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/appsettings.json (add Dispatcher:Enabled / Reconciler:Enabled / CrashRecovery:Enabled defaults)</file>
      <file role="modify-both">infrastructure/bicep/modules/l2-worker-appservice.bicep OR platform-controlplane.bicep (slot-sticky flags OR slot-only deploy)</file>
      <file role="modify-both">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md §Deploy Topology (document chosen path)</file>
      <file role="update">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-202-punch-list.md B11 row (annotate outcome)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="202" status="complete">Punch list B11 row + verification matrix — this task's scope authority</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task-202 punch list verification obligation">Executor MUST grep-verify `.Api` project split status BEFORE choosing path. If `.Api` already exists + wired → Path SPLIT is ~4-6h (finish wiring); if `.Api` does NOT exist → Path SPLIT is full 16h (create project + move endpoints). Path FLAGS is ~4-6h regardless. Choose based on evidence, not assumption.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF hygiene">N/A — L2 changes only. But any Bicep change that alters App Service slot configuration MUST pre-check LIVE App Service + KV state per project CLAUDE.md § MUST rules pre-check gate (FR-35).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-3 §5 alternatives">Both paths are architecturally acceptable per DS-3. Don't invent a THIRD path — the design study evaluated alternatives, these two are the survivors. If executor sees a compelling third path, escalate rather than invent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 asymmetric-registration governance">Path FLAGS uses `if (flag) { services.AddHostedService(...) }` pattern. If any UNCONDITIONALLY-registered service in Core depends on the flag-gated background service (e.g., a REST endpoint that requires the dispatcher be running to enqueue), apply ADR-032 F.1 Null-Object kill-switch pattern (P1/P2/P3) per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F.1. Startup should not fail; dependent surface should return sensible degraded response.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md § MUST rules pre-check">MUST pre-check LIVE App Service + KV + Dataverse before removing any alias (FR-35 pre-check gate). If Bicep changes rename/remove any slot config, run the pre-check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 Component Justification">Path SPLIT introduces NEW project (`.Api`). Justify per §11: (1) Existing overlap — `.Worker` currently hosts everything; (2) Extension — could keep everything in Worker + use Path FLAGS instead (that's Path FLAGS's whole point); (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing — staging slot double-processes production SB/Cosmos (concrete failure mode). Path SPLIT wins on architectural cleanliness; Path FLAGS wins on §11 minimalism. Choose based on grep evidence of `.Api` status.</constraint>
  </constraints>

