  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, opus/xhigh). Read `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B11 + verification matrix. Read DS-3 notes (staging-slot topology deep-dive). Read `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Verify `.Api` split status">Enumerate `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.*/*.csproj`. Read `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Program.cs` end-to-end — identify all REST endpoint mappings + background service registrations. Determine:
- Does `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Api` project exist?
- If yes: what's wired vs unwired?
- If no: how much REST-endpoint code lives in Worker today?</step>
    <step order="2" name="Choose path + document">Based on Step 1 evidence:
- If `.Api` exists + close to done → **Path SPLIT** (~4-6h)
- If `.Api` doesn't exist + Worker has significant REST code → **Path FLAGS** (~4-6h) UNLESS strong architectural argument for full split (~16h)
- If ambiguous → escalate to owner for path choice
Document chosen path + rationale in `notes/task-204d-path-decision.md`.</step>
    <step order="3a" name="Path SPLIT execute">Create/complete `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Api` project. Move REST endpoint mappings from Worker to `.Api`. `.Api` references `.Core` for domain types. `.Worker` retains BackgroundServices only (dispatcher / reconciler / crash-recovery). Update Bicep to deploy `.Api` to both slots + `.Worker` to production slot only (or Worker as separate App Service). Update `design.md` §Deploy Topology.</step>
    <step order="3b" name="Path FLAGS execute">Add three config flags to `Worker/appsettings.json`: `Dispatcher:Enabled`, `Reconciler:Enabled`, `CrashRecovery:Enabled` (all default true — flags EXPRESS staging behavior, defaults are safe-on for production). Add startup gate in `Program.cs` reading each flag BEFORE `.AddHostedService()` calls. Update Bicep `slotSetting: true` markers on all three flags in `l2-worker-appservice.bicep` or `platform-controlplane.bicep`; production slot values = true, staging slot values = false. Apply ADR-032 F.1 Null-Object kill-switch pattern for any unconditional consumer of the gated services.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Bicep pre-check + apply">Run FR-35 pre-check against LIVE App Service state (dev L2 slot config). Apply Bicep changes. Verify staging slot deploys with flags=false (Path FLAGS) or without Worker (Path SPLIT).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">Unit tests for startup-gate behavior (Path FLAGS: flag=false skips service). Integration tests: staging slot deploy does NOT consume SB messages / does NOT write Cosmos updates. Add ArchTest asserting no BackgroundService is registered without gate check (Path FLAGS) OR asserting `.Api` project has no BackgroundService references (Path SPLIT).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + verify">`dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.*/` — 0 warnings 0 errors. `dotnet test` green.</step>
    <step order="6.5" name="Quality gates">FULL rigor → invoke `code-review` + `adr-check` skills. Address any Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Report">Update `current-task.md` + `TASK-INDEX.md` + `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B11 row: `applied — Path SPLIT|FLAGS — <evidence>`. Update `design.md` §Deploy Topology with the chosen topology diagram.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger name="deferred-post-186" phase="Step 0">**GATE (BINDING per task 202 amendment)**: Task 202 amendment classifies 204d as POST-186 SAFE — staging-slot defect is ACCEPTED risk for first real run (task 186 uses production slot only). If owner directs this task run PRE-186, proceed. Otherwise DEFER this task until AFTER task 186's E2E acceptance completes. Do NOT start this task without confirming owner intent.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Step 2 evidence is ambiguous (`.Api` partially exists, unclear whether split intended vs incidental), STOP and escalate to owner for path choice — do NOT self-select on architectural judgment call.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Path SPLIT reveals hidden Worker→.Api circular dependency (REST endpoint needs dispatcher runtime access), STOP and escalate — the split boundary may need redesign.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any Bicep change would delete/rename a live-in-use slot setting, apply FR-35 pre-check gate FIRST + escalate per project CLAUDE.md § Human Escalation Triggers ("KV secret rename/delete without prior LIVE pre-check").</trigger>
  </escalation>

