  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`.Api` project split status verified in Step 1; path (SPLIT or FLAGS) chosen with documented rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Either: `.Api` project exists + hosts REST endpoints only + `.Worker` hosts BackgroundServices only + Bicep deploys them per topology (Path SPLIT); OR three slot-sticky flags added + startup gate implemented + Bicep slot config sets production=true/staging=false (Path FLAGS).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test confirms staging slot deploy does NOT consume SB messages or write Cosmos updates (integration or dry-run test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTest asserts BackgroundService registration invariant (Path FLAGS: gated; Path SPLIT: absent from .Api).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` + `dotnet test` green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`design.md` §Deploy Topology updated with chosen topology.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B11 row annotated with `applied — Path SPLIT|FLAGS — <evidence>`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 6.5 quality gates (code-review + adr-check) invoked.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): See constraints §11 row — Path SPLIT introduces new project + fails §11 minimalism narrowly; Path FLAGS is §11-compliant (extends existing Worker with config flags). Cost-of-doing-nothing named: staging slot double-processes production data.

**Post-186 safe**: this task's `deferred-post-186` gate defaults to DEFER unless owner explicitly directs PRE-186 execution. Staging-slot defect is ACCEPTED risk for first-real-run (production slot only); MUST-FIX before ongoing production traffic.</notes>

